WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.872 --> 00:00:03.020
Line 3 stands in hall B.

2
00:00:03.728 --> 00:00:06.247
That was the first of four projects this year,

3
00:00:06.456 --> 00:00:08.755
and the other three still have to start.

4
00:00:09.824 --> 00:00:14.259
The other three need the same two process engineers, and the same money.

5
00:00:14.995 --> 00:00:17.340
There is not enough for everything at once.

6
00:00:18.347 --> 00:00:20.344
Now you advise the plant manager.

7
00:00:21.164 --> 00:00:23.730
We follow that through the four topics of the module.

8
00:00:25.034 --> 00:00:26.833
The first topic is programmes.

9
00:00:27.559 --> 00:00:28.546
The readiness check,

10
00:00:28.709 --> 00:00:32.622
the planning tool and the materials process reach one goal together,

11
00:00:32.772 --> 00:00:34.142
fewer cancelled jobs.

12
00:00:34.893 --> 00:00:38.480
None of the three reaches it alone, so they form a programme.

13
00:00:39.528 --> 00:00:44.346
Line 3 is not part of it, because without that move the goal still stands.

14
00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:48.423
It belongs in the portfolio, all projects together.

15
00:00:49.436 --> 00:00:53.104
Each project reports green, while the goal does not move.

16
00:00:53.806 --> 00:00:56.941
So also report the goal’s own number every month.

17
00:00:57.932 --> 00:01:00.242
For programmes we use a programme board.

18
00:01:01.555 --> 00:01:04.667
The second topic is prioritising and capacity.

19
00:01:05.366 --> 00:01:10.138
The bottleneck is not money but the two process engineers, because they are scarce.

20
00:01:11.144 --> 00:01:13.466
So count their days, not the headcount.

21
00:01:14.253 --> 00:01:16.540
You cannot spend more days than they have.

22
00:01:17.599 --> 00:01:20.838
If a project has to wait, you do not just say no.

23
00:01:21.564 --> 00:01:24.605
You say not now, and this is what it would push out.

24
00:01:25.699 --> 00:01:28.532
For prioritising we use a capacity line.

25
00:01:29.819 --> 00:01:32.257
The third topic is governance and steering.

26
00:01:32.966 --> 00:01:35.323
You agree in advance who decides what.

27
00:01:36.118 --> 00:01:39.124
That covers scope, budget, timeline and people.

28
00:01:40.123 --> 00:01:42.840
The project lead decides within the margins.

29
00:01:43.548 --> 00:01:45.789
Beyond that the steering group decides,

30
00:01:45.998 --> 00:01:48.993
and anything that touches strategy goes to the board.

31
00:01:50.019 --> 00:01:53.827
The steering group has decisions on its agenda, not updates.

32
00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:57.241
If there is no decision, you cancel the meeting.

33
00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:01.498
For governance we use decision rights and a decision log.

34
00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:04.679
The fourth topic is benefits.

35
00:02:05.426 --> 00:02:08.527
The readiness check goes live, and that is the output.

36
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:14.371
Only later do cancellations drop, and the measurable gain from that is the benefit.

37
00:02:15.393 --> 00:02:18.203
The managers who run the plant own the benefits.

38
00:02:18.982 --> 00:02:22.256
Not the project lead, because the project lead leaves.

39
00:02:23.384 --> 00:02:25.973
The project closes and the team moves on.

40
00:02:26.691 --> 00:02:30.267
If nobody keeps watching then, the old way creeps back.

41
00:02:31.048 --> 00:02:33.823
So you follow the number for months after go-live.

42
00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:38.192
For benefits we use a baseline and a benefit owner.

43
00:02:39.545 --> 00:02:40.439
It connects.

44
00:02:41.144 --> 00:02:45.811
The programme bundles the projects, the capacity decides what can start now,

45
00:02:45.997 --> 00:02:47.901
and the steering group decides.

46
00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.708
The capacity line falls under the materials process, so it starts later.

47
00:02:54.436 --> 00:02:58.871
The steering group records that, and someone keeps following the benefits.

48
00:03:00.206 --> 00:03:01.890
This is the map of Projects.

49
00:03:02.591 --> 00:03:07.363
Programmes and governance is the first station of Portfolio and consulting.

50
00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:11.555
This module has four topics, each with four levels.

51
00:03:12.563 --> 00:03:14.932
Start with Programmes, at Basics level.

52
00:03:15.953 --> 00:03:19.970
At Working knowledge you add the MSP method, the capacity matrix,

53
00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.106
stage-gates and the benefits map.

54
00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.479
At Advanced you add the dependency register, cost of delay,

55
00:03:26.642 --> 00:03:28.500
pre-wiring and double counting.

56
00:03:29.544 --> 00:03:31.796
At Expert you add change saturation,

57
00:03:31.947 --> 00:03:35.662
zombie projects, independent assurance and the iron law.

58
00:03:36.672 --> 00:03:40.805
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
